EDGE COUNTS, two routes to e_H(L,R)
   m = 827: e(L) = 552, e(H[L]) = 576 = 24 x 24, e(G[R]) = 35, e(H[R]) = 1, e_H(L,R) = 192 (complement count) = 192 (degree identity)
   m = 828: e(L) = 552, e(H[L]) = 576 = 24 x 24, e(G[R]) = 36, e(H[R]) = 0, e_H(L,R) = 192 (complement count) = 192 (degree identity)

THE CAP AND THE PIGEONHOLE
   for a high z, d_G(z) = 28 + x_z with x_z >= 1, and
   |N_H(z) ^ L| = 48 - (d_G(z) - (8 - h_z)) = 28 - x_z - h_z <= 27
   m = 827, a = 3, tau = 1: w-contribution 4, sum over Z = 188, so each |N_H(z) ^ L| >= 188 - 6*27 = 26, hence min(a_z,b_z) >= 2
   m = 828, a = 1, tau = 0: w-contribution 3, sum over Z = 189, so each |N_H(z) ^ L| >= 189 - 6*27 = 27, hence min(a_z,b_z) >= 3
   m = 828, a = 2, tau = 0: w-contribution 4, sum over Z = 188, so each |N_H(z) ^ L| >= 188 - 6*27 = 26, hence min(a_z,b_z) >= 2

THETA ARITHMETIC, PER ROW  (t vertex-disjoint triangles)
   m = 827: theta(H) <= 24 + (9 - e(H[R])) = 32; each triangle saves one, so theta <= 32 - t, and t = 4 is the least that gives <= 28 < 29
        t = 4 gives 28 — CONTRADICTION; the residue to rule out is mu_1 + mu_2 <= 10
   m = 828: theta(H) <= 24 + (9 - e(H[R])) = 33; each triangle saves one, so theta <= 33 - t, and t = 5 is the least that gives <= 28 < 29
        t = 4 gives 29 — NO contradiction; the residue to rule out is mu_1 + mu_2 <= 11

